KNOWNBUG libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11 --object-bits 12 --unwind 8 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ the thread ran before join returned: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
g++ and clang++ (GCC 16 for C++23 and C++26) accept this program, and it fails
only its WRONG assertion.  The thread's function never runs: libstdc++ defines
std::thread::_M_start_thread (which starts it) and std::thread::join in its
compiled library, and neither has a model ("no body for callee").  A fix
models both, starting the thread with CBMC's thread primitives and joining it.
